DrugRef2 for CARLOS EMR — package notes
=======================================

DrugRef2 is the drug and drug-interaction reference service CARLOS queries over
XML-RPC when a prescription is written. Without it, prescription drug lookups
return no results.

Deployment
----------
It is deployed as a second web application inside the CARLOS Tomcat instance
rather than in a JVM of its own. On a single host that saves a second heap and
a second service to supervise; the isolation that matters is preserved by the
servlet container's per-application class loaders and by the two access gates
below. (The container-based carlos-podman deployment runs it in a separate
container, where the trade-off is different.)

Access control
--------------
DrugRef speaks UNAUTHENTICATED XML-RPC: anything that can reach
/drugref2/DrugrefService can query it. It is gated twice, and neither gate is
load-bearing on its own:

  1. nginx returns 404 for /drugref2 — the front door has no route to it.
  2. A RemoteCIDRValve in /etc/carlos-emr/tomcat/Catalina/localhost/drugref2.xml
     refuses any client whose address is not the host loopback.

`carlos-ctl check` probes the first of these from outside and fails if the
service is reachable through the front door.

Database
--------
DrugRef connects as its own `drugref` account, which holds privileges on the
drugref2 database only. Upstream's own configuration connects as root; on a
host where one MariaDB serves both applications, a drug-lookup service must not
hold a credential that can read the patient schema.

The drug dataset
----------------
The package loads the Health Canada Drug Product Database seed that ships with
CARLOS, but ONLY into an empty drugref2 database — reloading over a populated
one would discard updates a site has applied. The upstream seed creates its
tables as ENGINE=Aria; the package converts them to InnoDB immediately, because
a non-transactional table cannot take part in the backup's --single-transaction
snapshot and would otherwise be reported by every nightly backup.

Refresh or replace the dataset according to your own drug-data source and
licensing. Commercial Medi-Span interaction monographs need a licence key in
/etc/carlos-emr/drugref2.properties.

Updating the dataset from Health Canada
---------------------------------------
Administration > Update Drugref (in CARLOS) asks DrugRef to rebuild its
database from Health Canada's current Drug Product Database extract. The page
follows the run and reports how it ended; a failed run keeps the previous
dataset and says why it failed. The run takes 15 to 60 minutes, during which
drug lookups when prescribing are limited, so start it outside clinic hours.

What it needs from this host:

  * Outbound HTTPS from the carlos-emr service to www.canada.ca. The download
    is made by the Tomcat JVM itself (DrugRef runs inside it), so a host that
    only allows browsers out through a proxy must pass the proxy to the JVM.
    Set it in /etc/carlos-emr/carlos-emr.env and restart:

        CARLOS_JAVA_OPTS="-Dhttps.proxyHost=proxy.example.ca -Dhttps.proxyPort=3128"

    A proxy that intercepts TLS must also have its CA trusted by the JVM
    (-Djavax.net.ssl.trustStore=... in the same variable, or import it into
    the JDK's cacerts). Without either, the update fails during its download
    step, harmlessly, and the page shows the reason.

  * A mirror instead of the live site, if you stage the archives yourself:
    set DPD_BASE_URL=https://mirror.example.ca/dpd in
    /etc/carlos-emr/drugref2.properties (the file is read at Tomcat start).

The run's log lines are prefixed "DrugRef database update" in
journalctl -u carlos-emr. Every table the update rebuilds is kept as
<table>_prev until the run succeeds; an interrupted run (a service restart
mid-import) is rolled back automatically at the next start.

Deployment fix baked into the webapp
------------------------------------
The package installs WEB-INF/classes/hibernate.properties naming the dialect
explicitly (org.hibernate.dialect.MariaDBDialect). Hibernate's autodetection
runs a MySQL-8-only information_schema query that MariaDB rejects, and
without the pin the /drugref2 context fails to deploy at all; the file
carries the full analysis.

A second failure found during validation — DAO EntityManager leaks that
exhausted the 32-connection pool after a single drug search — is fixed at
source in carlos-emr/drugref2026 (branch fix/entitymanager-connection-leaks);
debian/drugref.pin selects a revision that carries it. If you build this
package against an older DrugRef revision, drug searches will stop returning
results after the first one or two calls: that is the leak, not this package.

Removing it
-----------
Removing the package undeploys the context and restarts the EMR. The drugref2
database is left in place; drop it deliberately if you want it gone.
